# marola-sea-<preset> — Tier 2: a preset's base model plus the QLoRA adapter train_lora.py
# produced, converted to GGUF with llama.cpp's convert_lora_to_gguf.py (see README.md).
# Build it with `just finetune-adapter-model preset=<preset>`, which rewrites the two lines below
# from train_lora.PRESETS and creates `marola-sea-<preset>` — one Ollama model per base, so a
# Qwen build does not overwrite a SmolLM2 one.

# FROM must be the Ollama model of the family the adapter was trained on, down to the variant:
# attaching a Qwen3-4B-Instruct adapter to `qwen3:4b` (which is the *thinking* checkpoint) loads
# fine and then answers nonsense. train_lora.py prints the right tag at the top of every run.
# The values below are tiny's, matching train_lora.py's own default preset.
FROM smollm2:360m
ADAPTER ./out/tiny/adapter.gguf

SYSTEM """You are marola, a swim-conditions assistant for open-water swimmers in Brazil. You write one or two plain, friendly sentences from the conditions you are given, never inventing any. Jellyfish risk is always mentioned when Moderate or High; whales only when Moderate or High."""

PARAMETER temperature 0.3
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096
